Z||000000||Justin||07-26-2001||10:26 AM||||I am 16 and am looking for my first car, and I have been looking at GT's. I found an 86 GT that seems like a good deal. Here is the ad:<BR>86 Pontiac Fiero GT, V6, 4 spd., AC, Sunroof, Alloys, PW, Cruise, Warranty. Avail..............Special Cash Price $1,999<P>It talked to the person over the phone, they said the clutch was just replaced, and it has 128,000 miles. It is red with silver striping at the bottom. It looks from the picture that it is in good condition. What do you guys think? Is it a good deal? I don't want to spend more then $3,000, so this is perfect. Anything I should look for when test driving it and checking it out? I'm really not looking for a project car, so I don't want problems to deal with.<BR><P>------------------<BR>If at first you don't succeed, pretend you were never trying in the first place.<P>visit <A HREF="http://www.twinkiesproject.com" TARGET=_blank>www.twinkiesproject.com</A>  for information on the chemical properties, reactions, gravitational resonse, and density issues of a Twinkie.||||reg||1
Z||000001||88CoupeV6||07-26-2001||10:40 AM||||Sounds like a great deal to me <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Good luck<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg">   <BR><B>Also 88 Yellow GT</B> :D  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||7
Z||000002||fierobaby||07-26-2001||11:41 AM||||well sounds like a good deal its a GT so it will be more but I payed $1,500 for my 84 Auto custom paint job 85 or 86 deck lid with wing and the car has 87K miles on it .... so I'm thinking if a GT is what you want and thats a good condtion GT its a good deal||||reg||1
Z||000003||87GTBro||07-26-2001||02:53 PM||||Give them $1750.  I bought my 86 GT (same color pattern as yours) for that much.  The seller wanted 2500 for it.<P>It had 144,000 miles on it at the time and was not in running condition.<P>Offer them 1600 and they may compromise around 1750.  You never know.<P>------------------<BR>AOL IM: GTFiero86Dan<BR>'86 GT 4 speed<BR>'87 GT Auto<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/87GTBrosig1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroKyle||07-26-2001||03:05 PM||||Seems pretty good. My first car is the 85 GT i have now. I love it. It has the 4-speed stick also. Don't let yout buddies at school pressure ya into stuff. It got me into trouble....... HaHa. Know what too? Your always proudest of your first car. I like love my car way to much, people say I have gone nuts. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sign_1.jpg">  <P>My Fast 'n Black Car<BR>AOL Name: Yakty Yak<BR>E-Mail: YaktyYak@aol.com<P>Kyle - 85' GT||||reg||1
Z||000005||Justin||07-26-2001||03:10 PM||||Yeah gotta stay outa trouble.  But there's this one kid with a Jetta that thinks he's so fast.  I know I can toast him.  He's not that good of a driver.  I was looking at an 87 Camaro IROC Z28 with a V8 and five speed, but my Dad said he didn't want me splattered all over the road so he talked me out of such a fast car.  What he doesn't know is that GT's are fast too..... Muhahahaha<P>------------------<BR>If at first you don't succeed, pretend you were never trying in the first place.<P>visit <A HREF="http://www.twinkiesproject.com" TARGET=_blank>www.twinkiesproject.com</A>  for information on the chemical properties, reactions, gravitational resonse, and density issues of a Twinkie.||||reg||1
Z||000006||rogergarrison||07-26-2001||04:52 PM||||If it was an automatic, id want it for myself. make sure you check carefully some of the things that normally are seen in here a lot. ie) exhaust leaks, erratic idle/running, clutch operation. make sure you test drive it long enough with AC on to make sure it dont have any overheating problems.||||reg||1
